Concurrent fingerprint and password authentication for Ubuntu 26.04

Type the password at the prompt or touch the reader. The module supports
interactive sudo-rs on the controlling terminal and the socket-activated
PolicyKit helper used by GNOME. Explicit stdin and askpass modes use sudo's
native password prompt.

Each user enrolls their own fingerprint in Settings or with fprintd-enroll.
Any reader usable by fprintd can provide biometric authentication. The
package includes no hardware driver or user configuration.

Password verification uses the system common-auth stack. If the standard
pam-auth-update fingerprint profile is already enabled, the password
verifier skips that profile in its own PAM transaction. The original file
stays in use by other services. Both authentication prompts have no time
limit. Fingerprint verification allows three unsuccessful scans.
Custom mandatory common-auth rules continue through the system PAM stack.

Run sudo apt install ./PACKAGE.deb to install. Check the terminal with
sudo -k && sudo -v and the GNOME dialog with pkexec /usr/bin/true.
Run sudo apt remove fingerprint-auth-choice to restore the original PAM files.

Native build on amd64 or arm64 with GCC, dpkg-dev and libpam0g-dev
  sh build.sh .

Cross-build from amd64 with the Ubuntu aarch64 cross compiler and arm64
libpam development libraries
  TARGET_ARCH=arm64 CC=aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc STRIP=aarch64-linux-gnu-strip \
    sh build.sh . /path/to/libpam/include
